  {
    "name": "verticals 314: at-risk keeps Medium and above only",
    "source": "tasks-verticals.test.ts:314 drift: overdue + at-risk surface Medium+ only; focus orders them",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "crit",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/tasks",
        "as": "A",
        "body": {
          "title": "overdue-critical",
          "priority": 5,
          "dueAt": "2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
        },
        "expect": {
          "status": 201
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "some",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/tasks",
        "as": "A",
        "body": {
          "title": "overdue-someday",
          "priority": 1,
          "dueAt": "2000-01-02T00:00:00.000Z"
        },
        "expect": {
          "status": 201
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "overdue",
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/tasks/overdue",
        "as": "A",
        "expect": {
          "body": {
            "tasks": [
              {
                "title": "overdue-critical"
              },
              {
                "title": "overdue-someday"
              }
            ]
          },
          "status": 200
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "risk",
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/tasks/at-risk",
        "as": "A",
        "expect": {
          "body": {
            "tasks": [
              {
                "title": "overdue-critical"
              }
            ]
          },
          "status": 200
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "focus",
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/api/tasks/focus",
        "as": "A",
        "expect": {
          "status": 200
        }
      }
    ],
    "note": "Read through the drift routes. Overdue has no priority filter (both tasks show); at-risk drops the Someday task, which is what the test asserts. The test does not assert the focus order, so the case only compares both servers' focus answers."
  },
  {
    "name": "verticals 241: the worker role may insert and update tasks, nothing more",
    "source": "tasks-verticals.test.ts:241 jarvis_worker_runtime holds INSERT and UPDATE on app.tasks (recurrence grant)",
    "seed": [
      "insert into app.task_lists (id, owner_user_id, name) values ('20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','{{userA}}','Personal')",
      "insert into app.tasks (id, owner_user_id, title, status, list_id) values ('30000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','{{userA}}','User A seeded private task','todo','20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001')"
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "grants",
        "sql": "select has_table_privilege('jarvis_worker_runtime','app.tasks','INSERT') as can_insert, has_table_privilege('jarvis_worker_runtime','app.tasks','UPDATE') as can_update, has_table_privilege('jarvis_worker_runtime','app.tasks','TRUNCATE') as can_truncate",
        "as": "A",
        "expect": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "can_insert": true,
              "can_update": true,
              "can_truncate": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "worker inserts for its actor",
        "sql": "insert into app.tasks (id, owner_user_id, title, list_id) select gen_random_uuid(), '{{userA}}', 'worker made', id from app.task_lists limit 1",
        "as": "A",
        "role": "worker",
        "expect": {
          "affected": [1]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "worker updates own",
        "sql": "update app.tasks set title = 'worker renamed'",
        "as": "A",
        "role": "worker",
        "expect": {
          "affected": [1]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "negative control: worker updates as a stranger",
        "sql": "update app.tasks set title = 'taken'",
        "as": "B",
        "role": "worker",
        "expect": {
          "affected": [0]
        }
      }
    ],
    "note": "The test reads the grant table as the superuser. The case asks the same question with has_table_privilege and adds real worker-role writes with a stranger control."
  }
]
